{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Restore us</b> — The meaning is that the poet speaks in the voice of Israel in our exile. Just as You restored the fortunes of Jacob in the Second Temple, restore us now as well." "<b>You annulled Your anger</b> — In parallel to gathering up all Your wrath."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 85, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:04.406731602Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}